% co-authors; the entry itself carries only these first three and no note
% field in this file records the rest. Fabricating ~197 names to fill out an
% APA7 first-19-plus-ellipsis-plus-final-author list is not an option, so the
% trailing "and others" is kept: it is biblatex's own documented pseudo-name
% for an incomplete author list (see biblatex.def, \newbibmacro*{list:andothers}
% and \newbibmacro*{name:andothers}, and apa.bbx's \ifmorenames branch in
% \DeclareNameFormat{apaauthor}), confirmed against this machine's installed
% biblatex/biber (2.22) to compile without error or warning under both the
% biber and bibtex backends. Because fewer than \maxprtauth (20, APA7's
% threshold) real names are present, biblatex-apa cannot apply the strict
% APA 9.8 ellipsis-plus-final-author form and instead prints "et al." after
% the three verified authors -- a known, accepted degradation given the data
% actually available here, not a bibliography defect to "fix" by guessing
% names.
